{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset","id":1170418,"title":"If you could change the Solar Charmset","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-25T07:00:25-08:00","id":1170418,"title":"If you could change the Solar Charmset","content":"<b>What are the greatest strengths and weaknesses of the Solar Charmset, and how would you change it if you could?</b><br /> <br /> The reason I'm asking is because I'm working on a Solar conversion for <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1078625-ex3-machineborn-an-alternative-setting-to-exalted-third-edition\">Machineborn</a> and I don't think that simply referencing corebook Charms is fun. I could use the opportunity to try to improve the Solar Charms instead. I've already done some changes to prevent bloat and to alter effects to match the balance of my own setting, but I'm aware that some people have strong opinions about certain aspects of the Solar Charmset and I'm curious to know what these opinions are and if I can address them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T07:54:03-08:00","id":1170426,"title":"","content":"The Craft Charms, as so many others have pointed out, are in desperate need of reconsideration, and Integrity is an utter jumble. I just rechecked, and Words-as-Worshop Method has 14 prerequisites (I drew Charm Trees for the 3e Abilities to get some practice with Keynote).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T07:59:33-08:00","id":1170430,"title":"","content":"Move personas to larceny. Increase wars stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T16:13:20-08:00","id":1170544,"title":"","content":"More war, streamlining a few charms that should just be passive or repurchase upgrades...<br /> But little else to be frank. Most of them are sound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T16:26:32-08:00","id":1170546,"title":"","content":"Probably remove the &quot;you can seduce characters for whom seduction attempts is an unacceptable influence&quot; clause from Rose-Lipped Seduction Style, nix Celestial Bliss Trick (or replace it with something less prone to inciting endless flamewars) and a few other stinkers, include more War Charms... otherwise I'm drawing a blank. Something something clarity, something something natural language, I dunno (never really had a problem with that, but since a pretty loud part of the fanbase does, you may want to do something about it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T16:30:21-08:00","id":1170547,"title":"","content":"Craft has some clear problems that have come up in play for a lot of people - myself included, and I've seen other PCs in games I've been in face the same problem. The more Craft charms you have... the less you craft. You go from the guy who's always building interesting things, to the guy who does nothing, then suddenly generates an artifact.<br /> <br /> Other than that, nearly all the charmsets are frankly great. I would change war, but I'm not fond of the war system (battle groups just arent fun to command), but that's more a system problem than a charmset problem. Investigation is the only other one I feel needs changed. Not to any existing charm, they're great, besides maaaybe Mind Manse Meditation, but the charmset is just... tiny. Did you know Investigation has the least charms of any ability? As low as War is, about 9 charms less than the next lowest. I've been writing up solar investigation charms in my spare time to expand the charmset and build off of what's there, since I think it'd be a wonderful ability and very appealing supernal with just a little more content to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T16:40:59-08:00","id":1170551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset#post1170418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>What are the greatest strengths and weaknesses of the Solar Charmset, and how would you change it if you could?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I would remove the whole Charm system and replace with something simpler, like the Mage spheres system. I hate spending so much time checking every single charm for what it does, even 15 of them make the game a mess of constant skimming though the manual. Exalted is born with emphasis on coreography and narration, I'd have more of that and less rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T20:03:28-08:00","id":1170578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1170551#post1170551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would remove the whole Charm system and replace with something simpler, like the Mage spheres system. I hate spending so much time checking every single charm for what it does, even 15 of them make the game a mess of constant skimming though the manual. Exalted is born with emphasis on coreography and narration, I'd have more of that and less rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually jumped into the thread to post exactly this.<br /> <br /> I would love to have something like a row for each Ability (or action type, for Lunars and the like) and a column for each modification. Much along the lines of the Arcana and Practices. <br /> <br /> This could become the replacement of one mess with another mess, so let me explain what I'd like to see.<br /> <br /> So, for example, we could see that in Melee, we would have a Charm that changes your Defense, and a Charm that doubles your Withering Damage, and a Charm that lets you resist Overwhelming. Melee would be the analog to the Arcanum, while the Defense, Withering Damage, and Overwhelming Resistance would be analogs to the Practices.<br /> <br /> Since this turns into a bit of a grid naturally, we could see right away what the shape of the &quot;trees&quot; might be. What's missing, what's redundant, what might be good places to work in an Evocation, and so on. It would also give a good hint how expensive something should be, if a new Charm or Evocation was made and added. <br /> <br /> And we could also see visually what an Ability is meant to be good at all across the game line. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'd also really like a rethink on Charms that are triggered by weird conditions, like rolling a Yahtzee in your successes. And about a Charm resetting after certain things happen a certain number of times. That's basically writing a Charm to be forgotten during play, or if not forgotten then to bog the game down with book lookups. I can't imagine being able to keep up with multiple Charm sets in detail, in any sort of mixed Circle game. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, nonstandard rounding (sometimes round up, sometimes round down) needs to be nuked.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I have one last idea for this post, but it's half baked so far. (It's baking as my home table does some more playtesting!) I wish we had some sort of board or play sheet or &quot;heads-up-display&quot; view of what a turn looks like. Every place where the rules can be modified would have a spot where a matching Charm Card could be clipped or filled in, and that would show you exactly what you're rolling and what the results turn into - and if you trigger any funky alternate rules or Charm opportunities. <br /> <br /> In my head it looks sort of like a diagram on a Blackjack table, with places to put all your Charm cards: When you elect to activate a Charm in your upcoming turn, you can put your Essence tokens on top of those cards, and then as you work through your roll you have a visual reference for all of the modifiers you're invoking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T20:57:13-08:00","id":1170587,"title":"","content":"I think the biggest thing to address in general, is standardizing effects. The game presents quite a few standard dice-trick options, and then way too many Charms invent brand new ones. Especially dump any that involve rerolling dice, or rolling more dice as the bonus, because that's annoyingly slow. I'd rather a Charm give me double 9s and says I can't botch the action being boosted, than reroll 1s until none appear. It's not the WoD were 1s subtract successes and eliminating them is useful beyond negating being able to botch a roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T23:32:16-08:00","id":1170611,"title":"","content":"<b>Strengths</b><br /> I personally like that different Aiblities value different dice effects more. For instance, in Craft and Awareness, you basically see things going all-out, while in Melee you see some things limited since if they had every single dice trick as easy as those first two, it'd break the system in half. I also am one who thinks that some Abilities having some pretty cool &quot;to themselves&quot; takes is pretty neat, like the &quot;roll a straight&quot; one in Melee, or the Occult one needing a 666. I like the variety of dice tricks a bit myself since it helps in giving Abilities different feels, and knowing that there is a toolbox of them helps I think for the game's future development, as some effects the Solar ones touch on might make for good stuff to distinguish other Exalted for instance. I could see a Chosen of the Dice being all about risky effects that cause cool effects on doubles, straights, and all that.<br /> <br /> Tied to this a bit is how the use of some mechanics are not shared as a way to distinguish Abilities too. Melee doens't have thes ame toolkit as Brawl, as Thrown, as and so on. Presence does different stuff from Performance, even if they apply to similar rolls in game. Things like that I find pretty cool and interesting.<br /> <br /> I like how exotic Solar Charms can get in 3e, but still to some extent fill in aspects of &quot;Badass events characters in movies and literature do as being really smart, powerful people.&quot; God-King Shrike to me is like the scientist who figures out a disastor is coming and has to warn people. Dual-Magnus Prana has this feel of trying to repliate some of my favorite scenes in heist films. The Persona stuff in Socialize reminds me of things like <b>The Great Gatsby</b> or <b>Fight Club</b>. So generally cool stuff there too.<br /> <br /> Exalted since 1e is about the kind of widgety feel fo Charms and I'm not myself of the feeling that it does it service to go to something freeform. The combat engine is interesting, but I think that it doesn't really by design lend itself to something more Mage-like, which has a very stripped down overall resolution system before magic (Chronicles of Darkness at the end of the day is a system without a lot of wiggle room in itself and I think this shows with how powers can break it so easy or get repetetive in otherw ays at times). Anything freeform or standardizeda st talked above probably results in a fundamentally different game from what the Exalted system we have.<br /> <br /> I like that Charm trees are deep and have a lot of Charms as an idea myself. The 3e Charmset has this thing to me I like wherein two characters can Supernal an Ability and probably have pretty different takes on it or depths. I like how most Abilities have a vareity of avenues and themes to them to explore, which also helps in this. Even Abilities like Dodge have things to support the nimble character who gets in and out of fights versus one who cranks her Evasion up, or one who fights this kind of &quot;Initiative sink&quot; style.<br /> <br /> <b>Personal Issues</b><br /> So yeah, litany of issues despite I think perks.<br /> <br /> First, I think that while I don't think the system needs to be as mechancial as I have seen some fan rewrites, some interactions and systems should have been defiend ahead of time, more clearly, and with more formal langauge. Like, I like the bolding of <b>decisive</b> and <b>whithering</b> attacks. I like the use of she for user and he for target of Charms (I have a personal hate-on of second person writing that some rewrites try for). And I like the use of double-N as a term in places. I think more formal bits could have been done like this, such as:<br /> <br /> - More terms like double-N. Things like eliminate-N for stuff that is the &quot;roll N until N no longer appears&quot; effects. In fact, It hink that's the biggest one of &quot;Why wasn't this keyworded?&quot; for me.<br /> - Full Excellency as a term should have been defined in the Excellency section, not in Charm effects later on.<br /> - Similar on things like &quot;winning Join Battle&quot; not being defiend in one place.<br /> <br /> I think the definition of Supplemental and Reflexive wasn't stuck to enough and some effects could hav worked better with that.<br /> <br /> Some Charms I think over-estimate their effect, or at least in context of other Charms. This is an issue with Craft for me (see my houserules for more there as self-plug, hint-hint, nudge-nudge). Craft overvalues points on early Charms, undervalues them in later Charms, overvalues slots in general, and ludicrously overvalues repairing stuff.<br /> <br /> Some charms get a good mechanic and kind of run it into the dirt at the expense of other Charms. I Like like though that there are chains on that, but soem chains probably end up being expaned at the expense of others for still overly binary effects. Survival could have more depth in the survivng, had less in the Familiar buffing, for instance. I think Ride could have had more stuff like Hero Rides Away, less on charging around. I actually honestly think more stuff like Salty Dog Method and Seasoned Criminal Method would have been awesome around for more Abilities like Craft, Performance and such.<br /> <br /> I think a lot of upgrade Charms more and more are better just done as repurchase for wordcount reasons and for keeping Charm trees a bit less &quot;linear&quot;. I hate how deep Craft goes though at times pretty dry and &quot;upgradey&quot; effects that a character might not care to have all of.<br /> <br /> The Performance double-9 Charms kind of annoy me in a way that no other Charms do. If <i>all they do</i> is double-9s, they shouldn't be separate Charms. If they are to be so, I think most could have had soem of their &quot;follow up&quot; effects rolled into them. Make them &quot;Some thing and double-9s as a bonus&quot; and less &quot;Double-9s as gateway Charm&quot; as they are I think.<br /> <br /> I would probably get rid of effects that encourage decision peralysis. Like, my houserules simplify the hell out of Bright-Forging Prana. Rather than pile of Charms that you have to pick on a laundry list, just have a simpler &quot;power up&quot; effect.<br /> <br /> I would probably also get rid fo anything that manipulated the xp economy, though I don't mind the one in Craft to use wxp to fuel other Charms (that seems about what that shoudl be I guess). But the Lore tree probably could do with having its xp-manipulation shortened, or put somehwere in branches that will caues less havoc for STs if they want to keep them in there.<br /> <br /> Personas are a great idea. Their execution is terrible with their furthering of using xp as an economy for it and the way you build characters. I think it should have just...been simpler. I honestlyw onder if Personas would have done better to be built as a form of QuicK Character with simpler effects and Charms, rather than the xp mess they are by default. That's at least how I'd do it. Right now they're the worst of both worlds in the previosu two issues.<br /> <br /> There's a few Charms with an air-breathing mermaid feel, like the one to train characters with learning disabilites, which is also kind of a basis for too much other things. I think if a Charm implies something overly narrative in its basis, it shoudl probably be its own thing, or lead elsewhere. Or just don't put them in if they only exist to solve questions that the base system doesn't have resoultion for. Or make them just...do more if they do. Again, nothing wrong with more Salty Dog Method-style effects that consolidate ab unch of little things.<br /> <br /> Some charms have a tendency to &quot;rot&quot; on the character sheet after a point, not because they're replaced by better Charms, but their effects become increasingly meaningless as the game goes along. Brass Scales Falling si a good example of this. It doesnt's cale really at all, and later Charms and enough crafting makes it ultimately irrelevant. Charms like that should just scale a bit more in general I think.<br /> <br /> I think the weapon-summoning Charms could have been a bit better. THey feel mopey compared to just spending Merit dots on Artifact weapons. (My houserule here is they can be used as part of a Ready Weapon action or can charge weapons ala the armor charms).<br /> <br /> Multi-attacks probably could have done well to have just a general discussion in the core rules. Even if the base system doesn't allow them, they feel like something which shoudl be discussed in the base game's architecture. I think that most multi-attack Charms also might give too many attacks without some fall-back. Or by most I mean Melee's.<br /> <br /> I think Fivefold Bulwark Stance is too strong and probably shoulnd't be so able to negate like, everything.<br /> <br /> War and Investigation could have had deeper trees I think. I coudl see War especially havings ome neat strategy and such things. But I think that's where we need a more robust Strategic Warfare system than we have.<br /> <br /> Some Charms have some clause-based issues that could have been clearer. This is a result of them at times having this &quot;String of thought&quot; feel to them, and this resutls in what their total effect being not quite being clear. This goes with tigher writing and I woudl say that at times Charms in the 3e Solar set can be sloppy, for lack of better word on that front.<br /> <br /> And yeah, that's the gist of what comes to my mind. A lot of these are things I will probably at some point houserule for my games. Like...soemthing of a simpler Persona system really sits in my head there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":353,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","user":"Blaque","date":". 12-26-2017, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T23:35:11-08:00","id":1170612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1170547#post1170547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Craft has some clear problems that have come up in play for a lot of people - myself included, and I've seen other PCs in games I've been in face the same problem. The more Craft charms you have... the less you craft. You go from the guy who's always building interesting things, to the guy who does nothing, then suddenly generates an artifact.<br /> <br /> Other than that, nearly all the charmsets are frankly great. I would change war, but I'm not fond of the war system (battle groups just arent fun to command), but that's more a system problem than a charmset problem. Investigation is the only other one I feel needs changed. Not to any existing charm, they're great, besides maaaybe Mind Manse Meditation, but the charmset is just... tiny. Did you know Investigation has the least charms of any ability? As low as War is, about 9 charms less than the next lowest. I've been writing up solar investigation charms in my spare time to expand the charmset and build off of what's there, since I think it'd be a wonderful ability and very appealing supernal with just a little more content to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconding this though I do like battle groups personally. That being siad, if you ever post some of those Investigation Charms I'd like to see/potentially steal 'em.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T23:50:14-08:00","id":1170613,"title":"","content":"Shorter. Much shorter. Cut down the Solar Charmset to about half of the current number, and I suspect I'd still be running an Exalted game instead of a Godbound game that began as an Exalted game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T01:07:49-08:00","id":1170622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1170612#post1170612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seconding this though I do like battle groups personally. That being siad, if you ever post some of those Investigation Charms I'd like to see/potentially steal 'em.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still a work in progress, I've got 5 and I'd really like 7-10 (to put it around the same length as the other charmsets). I'll post a thread for critique when it's done, for now, here's the ones already written up:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/10al419Re8To4PZwAXftL-Q3vuiRksQbFGhsGv9wq3qs/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/10al419Re8To4PZwAXftL-Q3vuiRksQbFGhsGv9wq3qs/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/10al419Re8To4PZwAXftL-Q3vuiRksQbFGhsGv9wq3qs/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/10al419Re8To4PZwAXftL-Q3vuiRksQbFGhsGv9wq3qs/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T01:16:48-08:00","id":1170626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1170587#post1170587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the biggest thing to address in general, is standardizing effects. The game presents quite a few standard dice-trick options, and then way too many Charms invent brand new ones. Especially dump any that involve rerolling dice, or rolling more dice as the bonus, because that's annoyingly slow. I'd rather a Charm give me double 9s and says I can't botch the action being boosted, than reroll 1s until none appear. It's not the WoD were 1s subtract successes and eliminating them is useful beyond negating being able to botch a roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eliminating 1s is actually very powerful, as a lot of magic preys on them. Offhand - Hail-Shattering Practice, Fivefold Shadow Burial, Rumor of Form, Observer-Decieving Attack, Iron Kettle Body. Something like Excellent Strike in melee isn't just an accuracy enhancer that turns your average successes per die from 1 in 2 to 5 in 9, it also protects your attacks from magic that could hamper it like this. True, all we've seen thus far is the solar charmset, so how much the Dragonblooded, Lunar, etc. charmsets will prey on 1s remains to be seen. At the very least, though, we can assume Abyssals can do so just as easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T01:56:51-08:00","id":1170629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1170626#post1170626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eliminating 1s is actually very powerful, as a lot of magic preys on them. Offhand - Hail-Shattering Practice, Fivefold Shadow Burial, Rumor of Form, Observer-Decieving Attack, Iron Kettle Body. Something like Excellent Strike in melee isn't just an accuracy enhancer that turns your average successes per die from 1 in 2 to 5 in 9, it also protects your attacks from magic that could hamper it like this. True, all we've seen thus far is the solar charmset, so how much the Dragonblooded, Lunar, etc. charmsets will prey on 1s remains to be seen. At the very least, though, we can assume Abyssals can do so just as easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, my view as well. I think that Solar Charms show some of the potential dice tricks partially to introduce them as options for later splats. Solars have a good range, but there are some Exatls that might use some fo them more heavily and I think a good bit of the Solar Charmset as is (to me at least) is showing what thsoe are and some ways around their esponses. The interactions with 1s are a good case fo this.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T02:36:51-08:00","id":1170632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1170426#post1170426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Craft Charms, as so many others have pointed out, are in desperate need of reconsideration, and Integrity is an utter jumble. I just rechecked, and Words-as-Worshop Method has 14 prerequisites (I drew Charm Trees for the 3e Abilities to get some practice with Keynote).</div> </div> </div> </div>It has 8, not 14.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyhow.<br /> Rewrite charms to be clearer. Especially Athletics.<br /> Also, there's quite a lot of charms that could be made immensely simpler with very small mechanical changes. Considering how much time my players spent reminding themselves what their own charms did, that'd be nice.<br /> Make the ability prereqs slightly lower.<br /> Move dice tricks out of charm trees (I don't like them, but some people do. So keep them available, just not as speed-bump prereqs). <br /> Redo the whole Craft tree to be more balanced and more interesting.<br /> <br /> No charmset is perfect, but I think that'd solve like 90% of the issues. Obviously there's always going to be some specific charms I don't like, but a lot of that is personal taste, so the charms I dislike might not be the ones you dislike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T02:51:32-08:00","id":1170634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1170632#post1170632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make the ability prereqs slightly lower.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, this one, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T04:13:55-08:00","id":1170641,"title":"","content":"Since this is an unrealistic wishlist: Cut it by 2/3. Cap a given charm tree at 16-20 charms. Reduce starting number of charm picks. Increase XP cost of charms to 2x. Combine charms together into cooler &quot;bulk&quot; effects that feel meaningful. Thin out the number of charms that are pure dice manipulation and nothing else. Find another way to represent topping out other than an artificial dice cap, this is a fucking lazy way of limiting things that feels gamey as hell. Why has this gone unchallenged for 3 effing editions now? Excellencies are terrible, get rid of them please. Don't standardize dice tricks, I'm not trying to turn this into 4E DnD. Clearly define what the mechanical intent of each tree is if they are flavored (aka, brawl is primarily a 1v1 thing,etc). Offload a number of key charm effects into inherent caste powers so you stop getting people clearly trying to steal schticks from another caste's intended strengths and re-enforce caste roles. Shave the number of abilities down to 20. Make ability requirement the same as the Essence requirement of charms. Get rid of charm expansions that aren't automatic upgrades. Get rid of references to Essence 6 shit in the corebook, undermining your own stated goal at keeping the scale from 1-5 with 6+ representing personal powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T04:26:20-08:00","id":1170645,"title":"","content":"Simplifying for the sake of simplifying will not go the way you are expecting it to go.<br /> <br /> The number of charms is not a big deal, the little charms that feel like mere speedbumps are, far more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T04:50:51-08:00","id":1170653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1170645#post1170645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simplifying for the sake of simplifying will not go the way you are expecting it to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah man, I have no idea what I'm talking about.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T06:55:35-08:00","id":1170664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1170645#post1170645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simplifying for the sake of simplifying will not go the way you are expecting it to go.<br /> <br /> The number of charms is not a big deal, the little charms that feel like mere speedbumps are, far more.</div> </div> </div> </div>How much of his post did you actually read, like, did your eyes just see &quot;charms&quot; and the numbers and glaze over on everything else? He actually explains his logic behind the simplification. (you don't and haven't) It is categorically not &quot;simplifying for the sake of simplifying&quot; as you claim. You're not even disagreeing that much, ParanoiaCombo would love to see the speedbumps go away and says as much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T07:15:25-08:00","id":1170669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1170632#post1170632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has 8, not 14.</div> </div> </div> </div>Craftsman Needs No Tools<br /> <br /> Arete-Shifting Prana<br /> Sublime Transference<br /> <br /> Tireless Workhorse Method<br /> Efficient Craftsman Technique<br /> <br /> Ages-Echoing Wisdom<br /> Dragon Soul Emergence<br /> Copper Spider Conception<br /> Clay-and-Breath Practice<br /> Spirit-Gathering Industry<br /> Unwinding Gyre Meditation<br /> Exegesis of the Distilled Form<br /> Spirit-Stoking Elevation<br /> Vice-Miracle Technique<br /> <br /> 14 Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T08:15:19-08:00","id":1170679,"title":"","content":"Huh?<br /> <br /> Words-As-Workshop needs Craftsman Needs No Tools and Vice-Miracle Technique.<br /> <br /> Vice-Miracle technique needs Summit-Piercing Touch, which needs Ages-Echoing Wisdom, which needs Efficient Craftsmen Technique and Sublime Transference.<br /> Efficient Craftsmen needs Tireless Workhorse Method. Sublime Transference needs Arete-Shifting Prana.<br /> <br /> That's 8 total.<br /> <br /> Why would you need Spirit-Stoking Elevation and its prereqs? I mean, that's an Essence 5 charm! Words-As-Workshop is only Essence 3, that'd be bizarre.<br /> I think you've made a mistake.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T10:47:05-08:00","id":1170727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1170611#post1170611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Strengths</b><br /> I personally like that different Aiblities value different dice effects more.<br /> <br /> [[trimmed an excellent and long post ]]<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My main objection to having a bunch of special case rules is that it breaks the rule of thumb for human memory. Humans can (generally) remember 7+-2 things at a time. So, five different major rules variations will be taxing for some people to remember, while some others can keep up to nine. Very few people can keep substantially more than nine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T10:56:55-08:00","id":1170731,"title":"","content":"Some my players found easy. Double 8s, double 9s and double 7s. Re-rolling 6s, or 5s and 6s, were a bit more difficult. They could never remember which effects caused cascading re-rolls or just one re-roll though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T11:12:26-08:00","id":1170734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1170679#post1170679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh?<br /> <br /> Words-As-Workshop needs Craftsman Needs No Tools and Vice-Miracle Technique.<br /> <br /> Vice-Miracle technique needs Summit-Piercing Touch, which needs Ages-Echoing Wisdom, which needs Efficient Craftsmen Technique and Sublime Transference.<br /> Efficient Craftsmen needs Tireless Workhorse Method. Sublime Transference needs Arete-Shifting Prana.<br /> <br /> That's 8 total.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently, somewhere in the process of diagramming the mess that is Craft, I managed to lose track of having already mapped Vice-Miracle Technique. I still think Craft is an absolute mess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T11:51:35-08:00","id":1170743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1170641#post1170641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> re-enforce caste roles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree with some of your ideas, disagree with others, but this in particular I would be vehemently against. I already have plenty of games with rigid Classes and I don't wanna see Exalted approaching that direction. I'd rather have the opposite, as I don't feel Solars need Castes at all, it is just WW/OP obsession with with every freaking splat needing Clans, Tribes or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T13:24:10-08:00","id":1170755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1170626#post1170626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eliminating 1s is actually very powerful, as a lot of magic preys on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, to me, isn't a justification for the mechanical effect, and really gets back to the really bad design issues with 2e. Charm effects that exist solely to counter Charm mechanics, just turn into &quot;paranoia combat&quot; style mote taxes. If I'm activating a Charm to eliminate 1s solely to stop &quot;prey on 1s&quot; Charms, again, I'd rather the Charm just say, &quot;treat your roll as having no 1s in it,&quot; than have to go through the time of rerolling<br /> <br /> My post was &quot;standardize&quot; not &quot;eliminate.&quot; Charms should do cool and useful things, but there's no reason for overly complicated mechanics. Even <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar353_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"353\" data-vbnamecard=\"353\">Blaque</a> 's case about giving Charm sets (both internally and between splats) a distinct feel doesn't really work for me. I don't need &quot;roll a straight&quot; as a strange new dice trick for Melee to feel different from Brawl. This also helps make understanding Charms easier. If the point of Excellent Strike is to help protect you from Charms that prey on 1s, it's a lot easier to know that when it says that, instead of it being an emergent property of rerolling 1s until you don't have any.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1170641#post1170641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Find another way to represent topping out other than an artificial dice cap, this is a fucking lazy way of limiting things that feels gamey as hell. Why has this gone unchallenged for 3 effing editions now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have any actual suggestion on this?<br /> <br /> How do you represent topping out without a cap? How do you construct a cap that isn't artificial?<br /> <br /> Why is this lazy, how is it &quot;gamey&quot; in a bad way (since this is still a game and all)?<br /> <br /> I'd say it's gone unchallenged because most people recognize that letting someone boost their rolls without any limitation but how much they're willing to throw at a single roll isn't actually a good idea, and nobody has any idea that's a &quot;better&quot; limitation instead of a equal if different limitation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't standardize dice tricks, I'm not trying to turn this into 4E DnD. </div> </div> </div>One doesn't have anything to do with the other. The point of standardizing dice tricks is to make the game easier to learn and thus more fun to play. Having every dice trick function under unique rules, even with the rest of your suggestion, still makes the game harder to understand and thus less fun for people. The &quot;don't make this D&amp;D 4e&quot; complaint seems extreme odd considering one of D&amp;D 4e's biggest issue is marrying mechanical standardization to niche protection... like:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Offload a number of key charm effects into inherent caste powers so you stop getting people clearly trying to steal schticks from another caste's intended strengths and re-enforce caste roles. </div> </div> </div>If you don't want D&amp;D 4e, you don't want the niche protection in the Castes to be stronger, you want them to be weaker. Stronger niche protection means you're turning each Caste into something closer to the D&amp;D 4e Classes with dedicate roles that other people intruding on ruins the synergy of the group.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1170743#post1170743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd rather have the opposite, as I don't feel Solars need Castes at all, it is just WW/OP obsession with with every freaking splat needing Clans, Tribes or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't really fair. Strong character archetypes backed up with mechanics isn't some &quot;obsession&quot; with some sort of vestigial design quirk. It's a regular tool in the designer kit that most RPGs use because it's a useful design element in lots of ways. I will admit that most of those benefits are aimed more at newer players, but that's fine by me. New people are targets for the books too, and they need more help getting into the game. Those of us that started playing Exalted with just the 1e Corebook have the buy-in and experience to help us house rule stuff if we want to remove elements like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T15:04:40-08:00","id":1170779,"title":"","content":"My Basic Gripes with the Solar Charm Trees:<ul><li>Too many &quot;repurchases&quot;, just grind that down into automatic upgrades at the relevant integers (Ability and Charm Requirements).</li> <li>Survival needs a focus other than pets, something that pulls on the powers of the environment they are in, yes that steps on dragonblooded a little, but they already step on sidereals and other splats.</li> <li>Occult needs more charms that deal with places of power, not just stomping spirits and enhancing sorcery.</li> <li>Archery needs more Firearms compatible charms, leaving firedust weapons to MA, is kind of a letdown.</li> <li>Craft and the whole damned system built around it needs a comprehensive rewrite (some may disagree).</li> <li>Stealth needs more cooperative charms, starting and expanding around Guardian Fog approach.</li> <li>War charms need expansions, I recommend drone warfare (summoning &quot;light bending&quot; drones ala Glorious Solar Saber and Glorious Solar Plate, and controlling them ala riggers from Shadowrun).</li> <li>The social charms need clarification of what sort of social action they are compatible with.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T15:18:07-08:00","id":1170784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1170727#post1170727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My main objection to having a bunch of special case rules is that it breaks the rule of thumb for human memory. Humans can (generally) remember 7+-2 things at a time. So, five different major rules variations will be taxing for some people to remember, while some others can keep up to nine. Very few people can keep substantially more than nine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I woudl argue the issue is less that there are a lot of effects, and mroe that they could have been worded at times more clearly or consistently. I don't midn thre bieng 40 Charms in a tree, as long as the Charms have clearer syenrgies and build-up and all that. System amstery and depth of mechancis isn't a bad thing to me at least since I like it in CCGs and TCGs and often remember quite a lot of stuff in those. Similar with some more complex boardd and miniatures games.<br /> <br /> I actaully think Exalted's not as bad as folks say in that regard, since in the end it's mostly mechanic dice manipulation. The issue si probably some templatiing coudl have been done and such to make that simpler, and that Solars probably were not the best place to go and try to showcase every single one possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T01:44:18-08:00","id":1170885,"title":"","content":"And multiple different ones in the same charmset. My players found remembering 35 charms hard enough as-is, but they found the dice trick ones by far the hardest to remember.<br /> <br /> This is the sheet I wrote for the Twilight when he was making artefacts:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 20 dice<br /> <br /> Flawless Handiwork Method (re-roll 10s)<br /> <br /> Bright-Forging Prana (1/story):<br /> <br /> [Supreme Masterwork Focus x3 (double 7s)<br /> <br /> Experiential Conjuring of the Void (1 success and 10 extra dice, all non-charm)<br /> <br /> Unbroken Image Focus (5 extra successes plus 1 per success rolled before double 9s, all non-charm)]<br /> <br /> So, in conclusion:<br /> Roll 20 dice<br /> <br /> 7s, 8s and 9s are each worth 3 successes, 10s are worth 4. For each 10, roll another dice.<br /> <br /> Then roll another 10 dice with double 7s (so they're just worth 2 each this time). For each 10, roll another dice.<br /> <br /> Now add 6 successes<br /> <br /> Now take away 4 (because the roll is difficulty 5)<br /> <br /> You need 100 total, and can't roll more than 6 times. </div> </div> </div>And that's not even working out how much gold and silver xp it cost to do that.<br /> <br /> Way too complex. Double Xs is fine, but when you've got a whole bunch of different effects on the same roll, the players just don't remember.<br /> I'm not going to be upset if DBs have a few charms that say &quot;double 9s on such-and-such&quot; or even &quot;re-roll 1s&quot; as long as they just stick with 1. Or 2.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ironically, in some ways, I understand why they did so many different ones in Solars. First, Solars are supposed to be the most powerful in their area of expertise, and are simultaneously most human, and thus are most likely to be rolling an attribute+ability really, really well. Whereas DBs or Lunars are just going to roll it a bit better than a mortal would (but maybe do something inhuman with it, like throw fire at someone).<br /> Also, of course, it was the first book, so they probably wanted to try them all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Some people have suggested cutting half the charmset out. I can see the logic, but I'd rather just move all the dice tricks into their own trees. Then people who like them, like Blaque, can still buy them, but you don't havee to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T03:29:06-08:00","id":1170893,"title":"","content":"Which is insane really. That's just silly.<br /> <br /> And also ridiculously powerful. It averages something like 39 net per roll. <br /> <br /> Personally I'd cut a lot of the trees wayyy down. I'd set a limit of two dozen charms per tree even, perhaps. If you can't write a charm tree that exemplifies Solar excellence in that number of charms, you should probably rethink how you're writing charm trees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T04:22:23-08:00","id":1170901,"title":"","content":"Well yeah, but high level craft needs a lot of successes (which I get the point of, though I always thought it could be done a simpler way).<br /> <br /> To be fair, players were really keen on having big charm lists, and when the old Devs announced that the book had tons of charms, few people said &quot;hmmm, not sure about that.&quot; Players were pretty enthusiastic.<br /> <br /> Also, there's plenty of trees that are okay in terms of number of charms. There's just a handful that are full of bloat, and Craft is the most egregious.<br /> I think that less the issue of how many charms there are is how many of them just do dice tricks, which people find really difficult to remember. If you take, say, Craftsman Needs No Tools, Players remember it, because it's &quot;the charm that makes me craft really fast.&quot; Graceful Crane Stance &quot;lets me balance like a kung-fu guy.&quot; Blazing Solar Bolt &quot;shoots a bolt of energy out of your sword.&quot; Players remember the approximate effect, which helps them remember the mechanics (not perfectly, admittedly).<br /> But with, say, Listener-Swaying Argument, which is the first charm of the Presence tree, players just go &quot;uh, some kind of bonus?&quot; But there's no in-game effect that helps them as a memory hook. Honestly, the guy playing the Presence-and-Performance barely remembers any of his charms, because so many of them are bonus dice (which aren't really bonus, because of the cap... except when they are) or dice tricks. And they have similar names to the non-dice-trick charms, so that gets confusing. Looking at the charm names on his sheet, he can't remember which are dice tricks and which actually change the way his speeches work.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say the number of charms isn't awkward at all, just as a matter of remembering them all, but I think &quot;give players less options&quot; is kind of complex. It's good and bad.<br /> <br /> I mean, I'd have been happy to have half as many charms and a book that came out much earlier. But now they're there, I find it easier to just not take the boring charms than go to the work of deleting them. Except of course, when you're forced to get them, as in many trees you are (frustratingly, since there was a deliberate point to taking excellencies out from the beginning of trees).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-27-2017, 07:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T04:43:43-08:00","id":1170903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1170901#post1170901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But with, say, Listener-Swaying Argument, which is the first charm of the Presence tree, players just go &quot;uh, some kind of bonus?&quot; But there's no in-game effect that helps them as a memory hook. Honestly, the guy playing the Presence-and-Performance barely remembers any of his charms, because so many of them are bonus dice (which aren't really bonus, because of the cap... except when they are) or dice tricks. And they have similar names to the non-dice-trick charms, so that gets confusing. Looking at the charm names on his sheet, he can't remember which are dice tricks and which actually change the way his speeches work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tried to make a Presence Solar once and had him know most of the Presence tree. I spent most of the time trying to piece out how many dice and successes I got from Charm X and Charm Y, then tried to calculate how some of the dice adding Charms interacted with my dice cap and how much I could spend on the Excellency. By the end of it, I decided to ignore using some of the Charms just to get a clearer picture of what I could actually do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T05:13:37-08:00","id":1170909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1170755#post1170755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have any actual suggestion on this?<br /> <br /> How do you represent topping out without a cap? How do you construct a cap that isn't artificial?<br /> <br /> Why is this lazy, how is it &quot;gamey&quot; in a bad way (since this is still a game and all)?<br /> <br /> I'd say it's gone unchallenged because most people recognize that letting someone boost their rolls without any limitation but how much they're willing to throw at a single roll isn't actually a good idea, and nobody has any idea that's a &quot;better&quot; limitation instead of a equal if different limitation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted has a fluid, character-dependent, and changing Dice Cap based on what ability you are using, with a further distinction between charm dice and non charm dice baked into the rules. This is actually really stupid. At every turn, the game is reminding me I'm a pile of numbers. Fluid numbers, which I have to keep track of. Some special numbers have an exception though to that number. Oh and don't forget non-charm successes. How many dice do they count as again? Ok just gotta remember that, it's fine. It's not as though I'm doing back-end math work to determine a limiter that would be invisible and non-player tracked in any game as math heavy as Exalted 3rd because any game this math heavy should probably be made in 1983 or as a videogame. Oh wait it wasn't? It's 2017? Well shit.<br /> <br /> They couldn't just put in, idk, a universal dice cap or something? Or do it the way every other game since the beginning of time does it, <b>and actually responsibly keep track of your interactions of powers so you know what the &quot;organic&quot; dice cap of your system is</b>. Man that sure would be hard with 750 extra charms you didn't fucking need, though.<br /> <br /> Quite simply, the game doesn't get to claim the game is a CCG style open area where combining effects and discovery is supposed to be fun, then put a cap on how those things interact to save you from having to actually do the math yourself as a designer and balance things. It's a safety net for bad designers offloaded onto YOU, the player. These kinds of safety nets work great when they are invisible and happen in the background of games. Having players track it is quite literally offloading unfun background systemic minutae onto the players, and reminding them their limitations are not bound by the powers they pick really, but by this number you (the player) have to keep track of at all times.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One doesn't have anything to do with the other. The point of standardizing dice tricks is to make the game easier to learn and thus more fun to play. Having every dice trick function under unique rules, even with the rest of your suggestion, still makes the game harder to understand and thus less fun for people. The &quot;don't make this D&amp;D 4e&quot; complaint seems extreme odd considering one of D&amp;D 4e's biggest issue is marrying mechanical standardization to niche protection... like: </div> </div> </div>You misunderstand why I jab 4E here. Standardization is bad sometimes in game design. Some system warts are, in part, what makes a system memorable. The fact that tons of people rejected 4E for an &quot;objectively worse&quot; system in 3.X and then 5E blowing 4E away like so much chaff seems to prove that standardization is not desirable in and of itself. That lesson seems lost on a lot of people for some reason. When you limit and don't standardize dice tricks, they become associated with a particular charm or action. It's easy to remember the charm which wants double N by exclude Y non success if it's one of one charm that does it, and that charm is 1 of 250, and not 1 of 1100.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you don't want D&amp;D 4e, you don't want the niche protection in the Castes to be stronger, you want them to be weaker. Stronger niche protection means you're turning each Caste into something closer to the D&amp;D 4e Classes with dedicate roles that other people intruding on ruins the synergy of the group. </div> </div> </div>Niche protection doesn't only exist in 4E you know. As a person who's primary concern is getting people to the table, playing the actual game, and not getting tangled up by the game getting in the player's way when they try to do things,stronger caste roles are simply a protection for that kind of play. &quot;The thing I AM can do XYZ&quot; is such useful shorthand for transference. If castes subsumed some of the important/iconic charm effects as Anima powers, you break the line of thinking that sees Caste as just another template on which you can play the character creation minigame. As far as I'm concerned, that is a good thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T05:30:55-08:00","id":1170910,"title":"","content":"I really don't like Excellent Strike. Three reasons for this.<br /> <br /> #1 It interacts badly with what people were familiar with from 2e, the number of people I've seen a non-zero number of people adding a full excellency and +1 success to a roll making an already extremely powerful charm even stronger.<br /> <br /> #2 As someone who likes the dice tricks, I think giving Solar Melee re-roll 1s so early undermines Hail Shattering Practice and takes a shit on Rumour of Form, two charms I enjoy for their last minute &quot;hang on there, you don't actually hit me!&quot; It also represents another source of unnecessary complexity from the same charm because the book isn't 100% clear on if you get to re-roll 1s before your opponent can exploit them.<br /> <br /> #3 It's still too cheap. I could abide by the effect if it was expensive to activate like the Jewel of the Rabbit Sword that required the Solar Meleeist to encounter and acknowledge that their opponent can use their 1s against them and to take a measured approach to this, but for 3m (it used to be 1) you can just go chop, chop, chop, chop and ignore everything.<br /> <br /> Some of these problems were things we noted in the playtest but I think I've soured on it due to how long we only had the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T07:00:35-08:00","id":1170931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1170903#post1170903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tried to make a Presence Solar once and had him know most of the Presence tree. I spent most of the time trying to piece out how many dice and successes I got from Charm X and Charm Y, then tried to calculate how some of the dice adding Charms interacted with my dice cap and how much I could spend on the Excellency. By the end of it, I decided to ignore using some of the Charms just to get a clearer picture of what I could actually do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering you can already buy extra dice with the cap, you probably weren't losing much by not using them. Frequently they just save you a few motes, or get the equivalent of 1 or 2 extra dice on a 20-dice roll.<br /> <br /> Actually, Harmonious Presence Methodology often costs you motes, if you overestimate how many presence rolls you're going to roll in a scene. I was going to get it, since it's a permanent bonus to all social rolls, and then I thought you know what? I'll just use the free excellency. If I make 3 social rolls in a scene, saving 4m really isn't as significant as something else I could do with 8xp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T07:08:04-08:00","id":1170934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1170910#post1170910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't like Excellent Strike. Three reasons for this.<br /> <br /> #1 It interacts badly with what people were familiar with from 2e, the number of people I've seen a non-zero number of people adding a full excellency and +1 success to a roll making an already extremely powerful charm even stronger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, definitely this. I had to remind my players several times of the cap, to their confusion and surprise. They still made mistakes. Honestly I didn't always remind them because I couldn't be bothered.<br /> <br /> Their views of the dice tricks' power (and, most significantly, their costing) changed a lot when they suddenly realised how they interact with the dice cap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> #3 It's still too cheap. I could abide by the effect if it was expensive to activate like the Jewel of the Rabbit Sword that required the Solar Meleeist to encounter and acknowledge that their opponent can use their 1s against them and to take a measured approach to this, but for 3m (it used to be 1) you can just go chop, chop, chop, chop and ignore everything.<br /> <br /> Some of these problems were things we noted in the playtest but I think I've soured on it due to how long we only had the core. </div> </div> </div>I dislike it too, as I think it's a dull charm you have to buy... but I don't think it's really that cheap.<br /> <br /> Even if you have 14 dice with a short sword, and buy 8 extra dice plus Excellent Strike, you're paying 1 extra mote to get, on average, 2.4 extra dice.<br /> That seems good. But... that's on a maximum roll anyway (maybe you don't have Dex 5, or it's a decisive attack, or you're wielding a tetsubo), and you spent 8xp to get a pretty marginal effect. It's useful against people who ram their defences up to enormous numbers, but most of the time, if you've got 24 dice you don't really need more.<br /> <br /> (I also feel the way the game expects people to have giant dice pools is irritating. And most of the dice tricks are costed on giant dice pools)<br /> <br /> <br /> Mostly, it irritates me that it's right at the bottom with Melee 2, because it's a charm for people with maximal dice pools wanting to roll slightly more than their enemies with their maximal dice pools. I kind of feel this should be an optional (ie not required for a bunch of other charms) charm for people with Melee 5.<br /> If you've got Dex 3 and Melee 2, it's a little bit pricy (and very pricy for the 8xp when it's just a tiny upgrade to your excellency).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T07:21:19-08:00","id":1170938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1170909#post1170909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Niche protection doesn't only exist in 4E you know. As a person who's primary concern is getting people to the table, playing the actual game, and not getting tangled up by the game getting in the player's way when they try to do things,stronger caste roles are simply a protection for that kind of play. &quot;The thing I AM can do XYZ&quot; is such useful shorthand for transference. If castes subsumed some of the important/iconic charm effects as Anima powers, you break the line of thinking that sees Caste as just another template on which you can play the character creation minigame. As far as I'm concerned, that is a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see your point about some of the other parts, but as Danelsan said, I don't think stricter caste roles is a good thing.<br /> <br /> My players are much more likely to have a good character idea, then try and fit it into an appropriate caste, than say &quot;I want to play a combat character, ie Dawn&quot;.<br /> The restrictions on caste already are too restrictive for them to fit their characters into perfectly (in fact, as Supernals and Caste Roles have made castes more restrictive I've seen this issue more); as you say, you want to get them playing without being tangled up by the game, and caste restrictions tangle them up.<br /> One of the best things about Exalted's character creation system (which, generally, I do not think is a good system, but it has some advantages) is that you can go &quot;I want to play a character who's good at Sailing, carpentry, Archery and writing poetry, which don't fit perfectly into one of a set of genre tropes&quot;. Compare that to DnD's class system, which is great at helping you make a character when you're not sure what to play, but not so good if you have a really original idea and need to fit it in. Hence why they need to make a million alternate classes, prestige classes, feat options, etc, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd be tempted to strip out castes altogether in any mechanical sense (and favoured abilities too). It'd just be much easier and simpler. But I do recognise that having some limits can benefit creativity. I think Exalted has a reasonably balanced set of limitations; not too wide, not too narrow. I wouldn't want to make it narrower.<br /> <br /> Now, I do see what you mean by the Character Creation minigame, but I don't think that's an issue with charms being available to everyone, so much as how 2nd ed's caste powers were just too random (most notably the way Twilights got an amazing combat power, rather than something intelligence-related. Hey, I'll confess, my 1st ever Solar was a Twilight just for that, and later I realised I'd made a bad choice). 3rd ed's are better (though not perfect). But refining them still further so everyone who wants an academic picks a Twilight and everyone who wants a diplomat picks an Eclipse I think is the answer (I think with this edition, the Dawn caste abilities are good enough that if you want to play the best combat character, you will play a Dawn. Same with sneaking and Night).<br /> Which is kind of similar to what you're suggesting, I confess, but not precisely the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T08:34:21-08:00","id":1170955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1170934#post1170934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dislike it too, as I think it's a dull charm you have to buy... but I don't think it's really that cheap.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's too cheap for a uniform charm without usage restrictions that can make you immune to someone else's strategy. If you only use it when you're spending +8 motes it's going to seem a lot more expensive and limited.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T08:57:23-08:00","id":1170962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1170955#post1170955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's too cheap for a uniform charm without usage restrictions that can make you immune to someone else's strategy. If you only use it when you're spending +8 motes it's going to seem a lot more expensive and limited.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's a couple Melee Charms that at times were written with too mucha &quot;free pass&quot; towards the Ability. I noted Fivefold Bulwark Stance there too, as it shuts down a crapload of strategies I think too easily. I think the disengage Charm in Glories is up there as something I'm iffy about.<br /> <br /> On dice tricks, something I think brought up I agreee with is that alot of them arise from ironically, standardization. Namely, free Excellencies and Excellencies being just a thing generically at the base fo trees means that effects whicha dd dice and such are not really on the table unless they break Excellencyc aps or do some circumvention with rerolls, double-Ns, and so on. Even keeping a dice cap, the game probably would have been better just tossing the idea of Excellency out entirely and having more things to work around in building ot the dice cap in combos as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar255_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"255\" data-vbnamecard=\"255\">ParanoiaCombo</a> notes, or at least have a soft cap in mind by designers and build Charms to that. (Though I would argue that's easier said than done in a game which encourages homebrew like Exalted does.) But making it so that you can't just out of the gate blast to your cap and then have to figure out what to do next would have helped quite a bit and probably would have informed the power of some effects like FFBS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T09:32:06-08:00","id":1170972,"title":"","content":"The problem is I don't trust Melee to lose its &quot;free pass&quot; because it's had it since the 1e core and going for non-standard dice adders could make the situation even worse if Melee gets a better opening hand than anything else, though What Fire Has Wrought may change my feelings there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 12-27-2017, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T12:46:47-08:00","id":1171030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1170909#post1170909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted has a fluid, character-dependent, and changing Dice Cap based on what ability you are using, with a further distinction between charm dice and non charm dice baked into the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>The dice-cap is also based on what kind of Exalted you are, and is one of those &quot;warts&quot; that non-standardized systems have as a potential positive. Your reasoning here is... very inconsistent.<br /> <br /> The variable dice-cap helps differentiate the different Exalted, including the Sidereals who have a universal dice-cap of [Essence] regardless of what they're doing. The fact that Sidereal dice-adding is detached from personal aptitude is part of their mechanical differentiation from the other Exalted despite being an Ability based set of Charms like the Solars/Abyssals and Dragonblooded.<br /> <br /> Differentiating between non-Charm dice bonuses (since these include things that aren't Charms, like equipment) and Charm bonuses is important for the dice-cap.<br /> <br /> Having Charms that directly generate non-Charm dice is of questionable design value, sure, because that's actually annoyingly counter-intuitive. But that's separate from the initial claim about dice adder caps being bad design.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At every turn, the game is reminding me I'm a pile of numbers. </div> </div> </div>Where, exactly, does this complaint stop? Isn't every mechanic in the game the relies on the pile of numbers the represent your character a constant reminder of this? Doesn't this happen every time you look at your sheet and see all the pile of numbers that is your character?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or do it the way every other game since the beginning of time does it, <b>and actually responsibly keep track of your interactions of powers so you know what the &quot;organic&quot; dice cap of your system is</b>. </div> </div> </div>Um, yeah, no. The vast majority of RPGs never actually manage this. Games that don't put some sort of limiter on things (which are rarely flat/universal caps) always end up with holes in the system that let one character roll 60 dice while 10 is supposed to be a lot.<br /> <br /> You're using plenty of words, but it ultimately comes down to a semantic shell game of, &quot;I don't like tracking variable dice adder caps, therefore it's bad game design because the game has me do it, &quot; rather than ever actually presenting a solid (on consistent) design logic behind your opinion. You can not like it all you want, but you can also just own it as an opinion instead of trying to make it sound like the design theory here is somehow aberrant and flawed because you personally don't like the result.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You misunderstand why I jab 4E here. </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but you seem to have a very strange take on why D&amp;D 4e didn't resonate with earlier fans (keeping in mind it actually sold well and has plenty of people that like it), and why D&amp;D 5e is doing so well with the same group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Standardization is bad sometimes in game design. </div> </div> </div>I've never seen standardization to be bad on it's own. It's only bad coupled with other things. One of the reasons D&amp;D 5e is doing so well, is that it standardized a lot of stuff that was overblown in 3.X, while making sure to not lose the play experience that 4e lost when it codified Class roles more concretely.<br /> <br /> How something is executed matters. Standardization is not good or bad, it's how you do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When you limit and don't standardize dice tricks, they become associated with a particular charm or action. It's easy to remember the charm which wants double N by exclude Y non success if it's one of one charm that does it, and that charm is 1 of 250, and not 1 of 1100. </div> </div> </div>This effect feels very overstated. The CofD has a set of standardized &quot;dice tricks&quot; that are used for (at this point) thousands of powers across all those monster types without all the monsters feeling exactly the same as each other. This is best (not always successfully) done by the designers that make sure the &quot;why apply this dice trick&quot; logic is consistent.<br /> <br /> And isn't this just &quot;off loading&quot; work on the players? It don't think it's fun to have to remember complex unique dice tricks to remember what each of my Charms does. That's off-loading making the Charms interesting on me, isn't it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Niche protection doesn't only exist in 4E you know. </div> </div> </div>Wow, really? I'm shocked at this sudden and marvelous revelation that I clearly understood in my last post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a person who's primary concern is getting people to the table, playing the actual game, and not getting tangled up by the game getting in the player's way when they try to do things,stronger caste roles are simply a protection for that kind of play. </div> </div> </div>Eh, it's a mixed bag, because players aren't a monolith. Some people like really strong niche protection games because they find it easy to get into. Some people, as I got beaten to pointing out, find strong niche protection overly limiting. I had plenty of luck over the years getting people to gaming table with games like the WoD and Exalted because they weren't strong niche protection games. There's some in them, but it's generally weak. You can play an academic Gangrel, or an introverted Zenith, or whatever, because the character creation and advancement is most focused on helping you make what you want to play instead of giving you a set list of what's worth playing.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T13:07:48-08:00","id":1171038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1171030#post1171030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And Stuff<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>All I'm getting from this whole thing is that Game Feel is not a design concern, to you. Conveyance isn't a design concern to you. The idea that Tabletop RPGs which require lots of player overhead could be considered &quot;work&quot; and not &quot;fun&quot; isn't a design concern to you. Only the system being consistent is. We have nothing further to discuss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":255,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","user":"ParanoiaCombo","date":". 12-27-2017, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T16:56:28-08:00","id":1171098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1171038#post1171038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I'm getting from this whole thing is that Game Feel is not a design concern, to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Game Feel&quot; in one of the more nebulous design concepts out there, especially for RPGs instead of video games. As far I as can tell, by any definition of the concept, neither of us is actually making arguments about Game Feel directly.<br /> <br /> So I have no idea what I said has left you with that impression.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Conveyance isn't a design concern to you. </div> </div> </div>Conveyance is extremely important to me. It's why I hate the idea of more unique dice-tricks over more standardized dice-tricks. Standardization of mechanics helps conveyance, because it's simpler for players to learn and thus easier for them to begin to understand how the different pieces of the game work together. The whole concept of conveyance in design is to provide the players with simple concepts they can easily internalize, so that they can more easily engage with the complexities of interactions of those simple concepts.<br /> <br /> Big bulky Charms with unique mechanics that do as much with 250 Charms mechanically as slimmer Charms do in 1,000 entries is easily worse for conveyance because you're eliminating the entry level simple mechanics to help players learn the game and understand emergent complexities at the same time. Standardized dice tricks, especially with clear design philosophy behind when to apply each (which the current Exalted Charms do not have at all), matter way more to conveyance because they make understanding the impact of Charms simple, so understanding how they combine in player is more intuitive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The idea that Tabletop RPGs which require lots of player overhead could be considered &quot;work&quot; and not &quot;fun&quot; isn't a design concern to you. </div> </div> </div>I've said nothing of the sort. I don't think it's an inherent design concern for Exalted, because Exalted is a game that has always catered to people that do not find significant player overhead to be a detriment to fun. I do think it is a general design concern, but it's one where you can't please everyone and you have to pick an approach and play to the people that like that approach. The nice things about games, is that one game doesn't have to be everything. There are games that have as minimal player overhead as possible, and ones that have lots. People can choose to play what suits their mood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Only the system being consistent is. </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> What is of concern to me in this conversation is <b>you, specifically ParanoiaCombo,</b> being inconsistent in your statements. You rail against the game putting overhead on players in one area, but then say the game would be better with more player overhead in a different area. You say that one rule is bad because it's too variable in implementation, and another rule is bad for being to consistent and standardized. You provide zero framework to reconcile these things on why these seeming contradictions aren't problematic to your statements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We have nothing further to discuss. </div> </div> </div>Possibly, but I'd like that judged on what I actually said, not you calling it all, &quot;stuff,&quot; and then making a bunch of dismissive assertions about my &quot;concerns.&quot; If we have nothing to discuss, it is rather clearly because you don't want to have a discussion where your opinions are challenged for not being the wisdom you're passing them as, not because of whatever aspersions you want to throw at your oddly constructed idea of my approach to game design theory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T17:43:28-08:00","id":1171111,"title":"","content":"Lots of interesting replies!<br /> <br /> For the sake of conversation, how do y'all interpret dice tricks as interacting with dice caps?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T17:47:59-08:00","id":1171113,"title":"","content":"We only have so many because it's so easy to reach that cap without any ohter investment and we probably don't need the sheer vareity of them if it were harder to make it. I think PC actually has a good point there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T19:16:36-08:00","id":1171132,"title":"","content":"What do you mean by &quot;interact&quot; with dice caps? I mean, they tend to interact by increasing your odds of success and/or average successes without using up numbers towards the cap.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing you mean to how Blaque interpreted it in terms of design. And I agree that the prevalence of dice-trick Charms is because Excellencies (at least for Solars) mean boosting your pools to max is automatically accessible. Charms designed to boost your rolls (as opposed to granting new stuff you can do, eliminating barriers, etc.) either need to be more efficient than Excellencies without negating them, or use dice-tricks. I don't think it directly leads to the variety of dice-tricks, or the Charms with non-standard dice-tricks in them though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T04:07:45-08:00","id":1171194,"title":"","content":"I'd say the solar charmset is in dire need of actual flavour and such, I generaly find solars bland as hell but seriously, pretty much every single charm there is some variation of &quot;You are better at X&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T04:45:47-08:00","id":1171203,"title":"","content":"Well yes, but, other than throwing about blazing bolts of sun-energy, making armour of sun-energy, etc, being &quot;better at X&quot; (where X is something humans can do) is kind of what Solars are about.<br /> <br /> I've found every single edition's Solar charms bland compared to other splats (actually, if you ignore all the dice-trick charms, this edition's charmset is actually much less bland than 2nd ed's. It's just hidden behind bloat. Charmsets like Investigation, Occult and Larceny are much less bland than before. And Awareness. Admittedly, Awareness isn't a brilliant charmset, because it's full of overly-complex charms, but it has some good ideas in, and it's way, way more interesting than 2nd ed Awareness!).<br /> That makes me think that's not an issue of Solar charmsets, so much as Solars themselves.<br /> <br /> If you want something less generic, play a Lunar. Or a Dragonblood. That's what I normally do (admittedly, it's a bit difficult currently).<br /> <br /> Saying this, I actually just made a Solar PC, but he's very... Solar. They do work best for a heroic paladin called Golden Hero who shoots demon-killing sunlight out of his sword.<br /> I also have a Solar monk with lots of Occult charms. The Occult charmset is one of my favourite ones, it's not very bland (though sadly I don't actually like god-plot, which makes the interesting charms for dealing with spirits less attractive to me. We're doing a good plot about ghosts at the moment though).<br /> <br /> (I have 45 charms on this new character! Ugh! I copy-pasted the charms onto a word document so I could find them easier, and rewrite them to include permanent upgrades from repurchases and other charms... and now my sheet is 12 pages long. Most of which is font 9.5. So I have some sympathy to the idea that there should be less, more powerful charms, that cost a lot more. But having less but more complex charms wouldn't help. Admittedly, most people don't make characters for a 360xp game. I assume down at low-xp it's much easier to keep track of your charms, but I never get to play low XP.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-28-2017, 08:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T06:04:42-08:00","id":1171212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1171111#post1171111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lots of interesting replies!<br /> <br /> For the sake of conversation, how do y'all interpret dice tricks as interacting with dice caps?</div> </div> </div> </div>The short answer is &quot;they don't interact. Dice caps are about how many dice you roll, not <i>how</i> they roll&quot;.<br /> <br /> The long answer is that as well, but with lucubrations on how they roll<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Glossary:<br /> &quot;Face&quot; is the number that shows up on a die roll.<br /> I will only talk of infinite recursions on the statistical significance of the dice.<br /> I call rerolls with keeping previous results &quot;Cascading&quot; and rerolls discarding previous results &quot;Negating&quot;. This isn't exactly what the game calls these rolls, but charms involving recursive rerolls showed these two behaviours.<br /> <br /> The dice tricks used so far take one of the following forms <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Increase the number of successes a face gives (double 10s, double 9s, double 8s...)</li> <li>Rerolling a face, infinitely or not, keeping or discarding the face that caused the reroll.</li> <li>Remove or add successes based on faces someone rolled.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> <br /> Without external mechanics that abuse faces (like the athletics charm that gives you successes for the 10s they roll, or the melee one that reduces successes for the 1s they roll):<ul><li>There's no difference between cascading a fail face or a success face, even if you cascade a face with Double successes.</li> <li>Negating is identical to cascading a fail face, but negating a success face clearly is very different, for you don't accrue that success.</li> <li>Sole exception: botches. Negating 1s negate botches, but cascading 1s only reduce their chance to occur</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Cascading a fail face reduces the chances you roll 0 successes: When you cascade (or negate) a failure face the possible results at the end of a roll include less fail faces. a standard d10 roll 1,2,3,4,5 and 6 as failure faces and 7,8,9 and 10 as success faces...60% of your possible end results are a failure.<br /> A roll with a cascading 6, for example, will end on a 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 as failure faces (rolling doesn't end on a 6) and 7, 8, 9 and 10 as success faces... 56% of your possible end results are a failure.<br /> <br /> <br /> Expanding the Doubles gives you a linear gain on successes per die: each double is about an extra tenth of a success per die.<br /> Cascading faces gives you an accelerating gain on successes per die: One face is a 11% gain from a standard die. Two faces is about a 25% gain. Three, 43%.<br /> <br /> With 2 Cascades and Double 7s or 3 Cascades and Double 8s you get about 1 success per die. 3 Cascades and Double 7s gives you 1.14 successes per die.<br /> <br /> So...the actual WORTH of those mechanics for the players:<ul><li>unless you cascade / negate more than one face, expect the cascade to be worth an extra die for every 10 dice, the same as the gain for each Double. Get to cascading more than 2 faces for the truly ridiculous gains.</li> <li>One non-charm die is about as good as gaining one cascade or increasing the Double range by 1 on a pool of 10 dice.</li> </ul><br /> I may have gotten a little carried away. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 12-28-2017, 09:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T06:31:11-08:00","id":1171217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1171203#post1171203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying this, I actually just made a Solar PC, but he's very... Solar. They do work best for a heroic paladin called Golden Hero who shoots demon-killing sunlight out of his sword.<br /> I also have a Solar monk with lots of Occult charms. The Occult charmset is one of my favourite ones, it's not very bland (though sadly I don't actually like god-plot, which makes the interesting charms for dealing with spirits less attractive to me. We're doing a good plot about ghosts at the moment though).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking you're mixing &quot;mundane&quot; with &quot;generic&quot;. Most of the solar toolbox is mundane, if extraordinary. Your offered contrasts are esoteric, and the implication that esoterism is how you create variety is odd.<br /> <br /> Can you really say every solar hero you can imagine is little more than a paladin farting demon blasters? Is every hero, flawed or not, essentially a morally upright person far busier with fighting evil than anything else? Is <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Snow\" target=\"_blank\">John Snow</a> so similar to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frank_Abagnale\" target=\"_blank\">Frank Abagnale</a> or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ragnar_Lodbrok\" target=\"_blank\">Ragnar Lothbrok</a> or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scipio_Africanus\" target=\"_blank\">Scipio Africanus</a> or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julie_d%27Aubigny\" target=\"_blank\">Julie d'Aubigny</a> that you can reduce them to holy warriors ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 12-28-2017, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T07:36:40-08:00","id":1171228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1171217#post1171217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking you're mixing &quot;mundane&quot; with &quot;generic&quot;. Most of the solar toolbox is mundane, if extraordinary. Your offered contrasts are esoteric, and the implication that esoterism is how you create variety is odd.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. I mentioned Occult, sure, but I also mentioned Larceny, Awareness and Investigation as charmsets with lots of non-bland effects. But being able to Sherlock Holmes it up isn't really esoteric.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you really say every solar hero you can imagine is little more than a paladin farting demon blasters? </div> </div> </div>That's not what I said. What I said is, I find Solars a bit dull compared to other splats, but I've made a paladin-esque character (he's a bit more complex than that, as he's really a Night pretending to be a paladin to inspire people, but anyway), and if you want to make a paladin-esque character who stabs demons with a blade of holy light, Solars are the best for it.<br /> They're also best for some other concepts (for example, the exorcist monk I'm also playing, the sorcerer queen my friend is playing, the master general my other friend is playing, etc).<br /> <br /> My point wasn't &quot;Solars can only be concept X&quot;, my point was, in response to the guy saying &quot;Solar charms are bland&quot; was &quot;I agree, but I think that's kind of part-and-parcel of being Solar charms, though they're better than they used to be, and there's still some things that work best with a Solar than other splats that have less bland charms, like Lunars or DBs. One example is concept X.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-28-2017, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T07:51:32-08:00","id":1171234,"title":"","content":"Gotcha.<br /> Also character count","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T09:05:40-08:00","id":1171247,"title":"","content":"Just a reminder that Sol is not just the God of the Sun. He's the God of a broad variety of things (including night!) and there's a lot of aesthetic to be drawn on there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T07:52:00-08:00","id":1171532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1170901#post1170901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, players were really keen on having big charm lists, and when the old Devs announced that the book had tons of charms, few people said &quot;hmmm, not sure about that.&quot; Players were pretty enthusiastic.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the same token though, there was a fairly positive reaction to Morke's statement that &quot;We're doing away with the overweight Charm sets of other splats&quot; (other meaning being &quot;Not Sidereals&quot; in this context) early in Ex3 development (see <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Charms\" target=\"_blank\">http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Charms</a> quotelist). The WW forum is lost to history, so can't give examples though! No wailing and gnashing of teeth when the direction completely changed on that though I guess. General reaction tends to try to be pretty positive whichever way you go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T10:39:35-08:00","id":1171563,"title":"","content":"I think that sentence needs to be taken in context though. It's discussing how the 3e design philosophy is (in theory) supposed to avoid the Sidereals feeling short changed because they have a set Charm list with ever other kind of Exalted capable of developing new Charms. It's not about the size of the Charm lists, but about what they can and can't do, and how much Charms should define a character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T11:36:51-08:00","id":1171576,"title":"","content":"I think I'd read it as generally against the perils of articulating a Charm set such that every possible heroic action is and has to be articulated in a separate Charm, with the idea that this has generally made the Charm sets of 2e &quot;overweight&quot; and specifically how that is a problem for hype of a character type like the Sidereals who specifically have a restricted Charm set.<br /> <br /> I guess I'll walk back my statement that they completely changed direction. I actually don't know the 3e Solar set enough to say if they did. There's ways that they could end up with the huge 3e Charm set while still having a weak correspondence between Charms and any particular actions (like, by just having mechanically many, many ways of doing things in the set that don't correspond to particular actions).<br /> <br /> (Still, I would stand by, the implication being of a smaller set and that no one was unhappy with the idea that the time, and there was a good bit of enthusiasm.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T10:54:29-08:00","id":1172028,"title":"","content":"A few more things. There are 3 charms with Masterful Performance Exercise as the prerequisite that give double 9s for different types of performance. They should be collapsed into one charm. Any other charm trees with the same sort of thing should have them consolidated as well.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d aim to get each charm tree to under 30 purchases total with repurchases worked out of the trees entirely. Each charms would have a unique effect.<br /> <br /> Lastly either limit the number of dice tricks to 6 or less or work then into existing charms. This would be a major undertaking though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T19:26:39-08:00","id":1175340,"title":"","content":"My thoughts (no idea if they have been mentioned or not - TL;DR):<br /> <br /> 1) Divide Descriptive Fluff from Mechanic Effect. If needed write the Description in <i>Italic </i>and the Mechanics in normal. That would accelerate ease of reference.<br /> <br /> 2) Keep Descriptive fluff MINIMAL. Give a brief description of what the charm looks like, but drop the poetry of &quot;The Lawgiver is a God that Walks Amoung Sheep, and where-ever they stride justice is planted in each footfall.&quot; All this tells me is that the writer is poet who wants to flaunt their gift in the wrong place. I don't need a movie director to make me an omelette!<br /> <br /> 3) Remove keywords where able (e.g.: Hanging Judgement Arc does NOT need the Keywords <b>Decisive Only</b>. Its mechanical description only describes a decisive attack. Get rid of these unneeded Keywords, or incorporate them into the description, and you are saving a TONE of lines of text [ -1 line from 700+ Charms = -700 lines of text])<br /> <br /> One particular pet-peve in this it the keyword &quot;Mute&quot;. Add this into the cost (e.g.: &quot;5m (Muted)&quot; ).<br /> <br /> 4) Organize the charms by PRE-REQUISTIES; not by Essence level. This again is terrible organization. Solar Archery is 2 trees. Larceny (if I remembewr right) is 4 trees. Having the Essence 1 Charms of all trees side by side make it hard to recognize the charm progression. Go back to the old editions where you would have Archery... and THEN divide the charms into their various groups.<br /> <br /> 5) Don't name RePurchase Charms that could be written as upgrades; For example &quot;Dust and Ash Slight&quot; can be written into &quot;Seven Omens Shot&quot; (e.g.: at Essence 4, you may repurchase Seven Omens Shot. This allows you to use the Charm normally, or shorten the long aim action by -1 Round to forget the auto-charm successes).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T20:36:57-08:00","id":1175355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenvious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1175340#post1175340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thoughts (no idea if they have been mentioned or not - TL;DR):<br /> <br /> 1) Divide Descriptive Fluff from Mechanic Effect.<br /> <br /> 2) Keep Descriptive fluff MINIMAL.</div> </div> </div> </div>these two are a perennial discussion, though overall people seem to prefer the opposite. I grok both, and rewrote all charms in bland functional mode for easier usage.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenvious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1175340#post1175340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) Organize the charms by PRE-REQUISTIES; not by Essence level. This again is terrible organization. Solar Archery is 2 trees. Larceny (if I remembewr right) is 4 trees. Having the Essence 1 Charms of all trees side by side make it hard to recognize the charm progression. Go back to the old editions where you would have Archery... and THEN divide the charms into their various groups.<br /> <br /> 5) Don't name RePurchase Charms that could be written as upgrades; For example &quot;Dust and Ash Slight&quot; can be written into &quot;Seven Omens Shot&quot; (e.g.: at Essence 4, you may repurchase Seven Omens Shot. This allows you to use the Charm normally, or shorten the long aim action by -1 Round to forget the auto-charm successes).</div> </div> </div> </div>These I can get behind. Former books had the charm trees drawn in their sections, which facilitated a lot.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T22:33:47-08:00","id":1175380,"title":"","content":"As a note, Charms are actually organized by Essence at least, and there's some benefit I think with things like, putting Charms with a prerequistie after that prerequisite.<br /> <br /> That said, something that really should have <i>also</i> been done was to split-up Charm trees into smaller categories like they did for Craft and Performance, as well as put a special header when they went to a new Essence level. When I sat down and did a personal set of docs I use for reference, that's actually something I did so I got something like, say, this for the table of contents for Archery:<br /> <br /> Clarity and Accuracy<br /> - Essence 1<br /> - Essence 2<br /> - Essence 3<br /> - Essence 4<br /> Speed and Multi-Attacks<br /> - Essence 1<br /> - Essence 2<br /> - Essence 3<br /> - Essence 4<br /> - Essence 5<br /> Sunfire<br /> - Essence 1<br /> - Essence 2<br /> - Essence 3<br /> - Essence 4<br /> - Essence 5<br /> <br /> And this for Melee:<br /> Offense<br /> - Essence 1<br /> - Essence 2<br /> - Essence 3<br /> Flurries<br /> - Essence 1<br /> - Essence 2<br /> - Essence 3<br /> - Essence 4<br /> - Essence 5<br /> Defense<br /> - Essence 1<br /> - Essence 2<br /> - Essence 3<br /> - Essence 4<br /> - Essence 5<br /> Defending Others<br /> - Essence 1<br /> - Essence 2<br /> Counterattacks and Clashes<br /> - Essence 1<br /> - Essence 2<br /> - Essence 3<br /> Summoning Weapons<br /> - Essence 1<br /> - Essence 2<br /> - Essence 3<br /> Ranged Attacks and Sunfire<br /> - Essence 2<br /> - Essence 3<br /> <br /> And so on. Basically the only one that I didn't do that with was Investigation (too short) but overall I do wish they had more of that around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T22:39:44-08:00","id":1175382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1175380#post1175380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a note, Charms are actually organized by Essence at least, and there's some benefit I think with things like, putting Charms with a prerequistie after that prerequisite.<br /> <br /> That said, something that really should have <i>also</i> been done was to split-up Charm trees into smaller categories like they did for Craft and Performance, as well as put a special header when they went to a new Essence level. When I sat down and did a personal set of docs I use for reference, that's actually something I did so I got something like, say, this for the table of contents for Archery:<br /> <br /> Clarity and Accuracy<br /> - Essence 1<br /> - Essence 2<br /> - Essence 3<br /> - Essence 4<br /> Speed and Multi-Attacks<br /> - Essence 1<br /> - Essence 2<br /> - Essence 3<br /> - Essence 4<br /> - Essence 5<br /> Sunfire<br /> - Essence 1<br /> - Essence 2<br /> - Essence 3<br /> - Essence 4<br /> - Essence 5<br /> <br /> And this for Melee:<br /> Offense<br /> - Essence 1<br /> - Essence 2<br /> - Essence 3<br /> Flurries<br /> - Essence 1<br /> - Essence 2<br /> - Essence 3<br /> - Essence 4<br /> - Essence 5<br /> Defense<br /> - Essence 1<br /> - Essence 2<br /> - Essence 3<br /> - Essence 4<br /> - Essence 5<br /> Defending Others<br /> - Essence 1<br /> - Essence 2<br /> Counterattacks and Clashes<br /> - Essence 1<br /> - Essence 2<br /> - Essence 3<br /> Summoning Weapons<br /> - Essence 1<br /> - Essence 2<br /> - Essence 3<br /> Ranged Attacks and Sunfire<br /> - Essence 2<br /> - Essence 3<br /> <br /> And so on. Basically the only one that I didn't do that with was Investigation (too short) but overall I do wish they had more of that around.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I like. This would have made things radically easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T11:29:33-08:00","id":1175516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1170418-if-you-could-change-the-solar-charmset?p=1175380#post1175380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a note, Charms are actually organized by Essence at least, and there's some benefit I think with things like, putting Charms with a prerequistie after that prerequisite.<br /> <br /> That said, something that really should have <i>also</i> been done was to split-up Charm trees into smaller categories like they did for Craft and Performance, as well as put a special header when they went to a new Essence level...<br /> <br /> And so on. Basically the only one that I didn't do that with was Investigation (too short) but overall I do wish they had more of that around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted a reason to rewrite my Charm Doc in InDesign so the layout was cleaner...now I have a reason. I also want to peel out a bunch of the speed bump and bloat charms without changing the overall charm design. Now I have a reason to do both. Anyone want to collaborate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T19:00:03-08:00","id":1175647,"title":"","content":"For me it would be trying to cut down on some of the charms in the book.<br /> <br /> A lot of them are neat, but I feel a lot of them are too weak able to be folded into other charms, likewise some charms can just be remade into repurchases instead of entirely new charms. I mean you could cut all of the charm text block out of Force-Stealing Feint if you just added an additional line to Searing Quicksilver Flight saying &quot;At Essence 2+, this charm may be repurchased in order to blah blah blah&quot;. Other charm trees I feel could have some charms cut out of them. This isn't for my sake (I actually like most of them) but rather for the newbies who get scared at the sheer amount of options.<br /> <br /> Oh and craft. Even just looking at the charm total, the dice tricks are way out of hand on it. I need a dice roller to keep myself sane on it. Double 7s is a neat gimmick, but when you're rolling that many dice in order to order to make some of the higher end artifacts I think the numbers on the base system should be reduced a little bit to keep things sane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}